module wvsd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.west-virginia.{ frcp6-west-virginia }

// The Southern District of West Virginia's own civil periods and limits,
// computed under FRCP 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule.
// Rules that state no period this layer can count stay out: the window of
// 30 to 45 days (60 to 75 abroad) the waiver request allows the defendant
// to return it (LR Civ P 4.1), a range the plaintiff chooses; the
// courtroom-technology certification 7 days before a hearing or trial (LR
// Civ P 7.1(a)(9), 16.7(b)(11)), a technology request rather than a
// litigation period; the court's own scheduling order timing (LR Civ P
// 16.1(e)); the mediator's report within 7 days after mediation (LR Civ P
// 16.6.8), a neutral's duty; the section 406(b) fee motion, due "promptly"
// (LR Civ P 9.6); the surety's filings after a real-property bond (LR Civ P
// 65.1.1); attorney admission, withdrawal and recusal practice (LR Civ P
// 83.1-83.8); and the Local Rules of Criminal Procedure. The earlier S.D.
// W. Va. outline's FRCP flow belongs to lit/frcp and lit/frap; its
// decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Foman v. Davis, Frow v. De La Vega, Celotex,
// Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Catlin, Bowles v. Russell, and in the Third
// and Fourth Circuits Phillips v. County of Allegheny, Fowler v. UPMC
// Shadyside, Poulis v. State Farm, Goines and Anderson v. Foundation for
// Advancement) are FRCP authority, and no reporter text is vendored, so
// they are removed here.
// In a Social Security review, opening and responding briefs "shall not
// exceed 20 double-spaced pages and the reply brief shall not exceed 10
// double-spaced pages, except with leave of court" (LR Civ P 9.4(b)). The
// rule states the count in a form the limit check does not read, so the
// limits stay in this note.
/// A memorandum supporting a motion, and any response or reply memorandum:
/// at most 20 pages; a motion to exceed the limit is denied absent good
/// cause (LR Civ P 7.1(a)(2)).
limit memorandum {
  pages <= 20 cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 7.1(a)"
} cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 7.1(a)"

/// The complaint is filed (LR Civ P 4.1).
event ComplaintFiled()
/// The defendant returns an executed waiver of service (LR Civ P 4.1).
event WaiverReturned()
/// A motion and its supporting memorandum are served (LR Civ P 7.1(a)).
event MotionServed() paper memorandum
/// The memorandum in response to a motion is served (LR Civ P 7.1(a)(7)).
event ResponseServed() paper memorandum
/// A reply memorandum is filed (LR Civ P 7.1(a)(7)).
event ReplyFiled() paper memorandum
/// The clerk provides the consent form in a Social Security appeal (LR Civ
/// P 9.1(b)).
event ConsentFormProvided()
/// The plaintiff serves the summons and complaint in a Social Security
/// review (LR Civ P 9.3(a), 9.5(a)).
event SocialSecurityComplaintServed()
/// The certified (or supplemental) administrative transcript is served (LR
/// Civ P 9.4(a)).
event TranscriptServed()
/// The plaintiff's brief is served (LR Civ P 9.4(a)).
event PlaintiffBriefServed()
/// The Commissioner's brief is served (LR Civ P 9.4(a)).
event CommissionerBriefServed()
/// The plaintiff's reply brief is served (LR Civ P 9.4(a)).
event SocialSecurityReplyServed()
/// The final judgment is entered (LR Civ P 9.6, 54.1).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// The date set for the scheduling conference (LR Civ P 16.1(b)-(c)).
event SchedulingConference()
/// A case-management conference in a complex case (LR Civ P 16.2(b)).
event CaseManagementConference()
/// The final pretrial conference (LR Civ P 16.7(a)-(b)).
event FinalPretrialConference()
/// The parties' Fed. R. Civ. P. 26(f) meeting (LR Civ P 26.1(a)).
event PartiesMeeting()
/// The discovery completion date (LR Civ P 26.1(b)).
event DiscoveryCompletion()
/// The court orders interrogatories answered over objection (LR Civ P
/// 33.1(c)).
event InterrogatoryAnswersOrdered()
/// The court orders document requests answered over objection (LR Civ P
/// 34.1(c)).
event DocumentAnswersOrdered()
/// The court rules a request for admission proper over objection (LR Civ P
/// 36.1(b)).
event AdmissionRequestHeldProper()
/// The date a discovery response or disclosure was due (LR Civ P 37.1(c)).
event DiscoveryResponseDue()
/// The judicial officer gives notice that an action will be dismissed (LR
/// Civ P 41.1).
event DismissalNoticeGiven()
/// The trial date (LR Civ P 51.1, 52.1).
event TrialDate()
/// The bill of costs is served (LR Civ P 54.1).
event BillOfCostsServed()
/// Objections to the bill of costs are served (LR Civ P 54.1).
event CostsObjectionsServed()

/// LR Civ P 4.1: a plaintiff who intends to obtain service under Fed. R.
/// Civ. P. 4(d)(1) dispatches the notice and request, and files a copy,
/// within 14 days of filing the complaint; otherwise service is made by
/// other means unless otherwise ordered.
deadline waiver-request-period: 14.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 4.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 4.1: the plaintiff files the waiver of service within 7 days
/// after its return.
deadline waiver-filing-period: 7.days after WaiverReturned() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 4.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 7.1(a)(7): memoranda in response to a motion are filed and
/// served within 14 days from service of the motion; the judicial officer
/// may modify the time.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 7.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 7.1(a)(7): a reply memorandum is filed and served within 7 days
/// from service of the response. No surreply without leave.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 7.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 9.1(b): in a Social Security appeal, the completed consent to
/// proceed before a magistrate judge is returned within 21 days of the
/// clerk's notice.
deadline consent-form-period: 21.days after ConsentFormProvided() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 9.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 9.3(a), 9.5(a): no later than 60 days after the plaintiff
/// serves the summons and complaint, the Commissioner files and serves an
/// answer with the certified administrative transcript, or a motion to
/// dismiss or remand with a supporting memorandum.
deadline commissioner-response-period: 60.days after SocialSecurityComplaintServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 9.3(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 9.4(a): the plaintiff's brief is filed and served no later than
/// 30 days after service of the certified (or supplemental) administrative
/// transcript.
deadline plaintiff-brief-period: 30.days after TranscriptServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 9.4(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 9.4(a): the Commissioner's brief is filed and served no later
/// than 30 days after service of the plaintiff's brief.
deadline commissioner-brief-period: 30.days after PlaintiffBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 9.4(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 9.4(a): the plaintiff may file and serve a reply brief no later
/// than 14 days after service of the Commissioner's brief. Responses and
/// replies to a motion to dismiss or remand follow the same periods (LR
/// Civ P 9.5(c)).
deadline social-security-reply-period: 14.days after CommissionerBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 9.4(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 9.6: the Fed. R. Civ. P. 54(d) limits do not apply; a motion for
/// fees under the Equal Access to Justice Act is filed within 90 days of
/// entry of final judgment.
deadline eaja-fee-motion-period: 90.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 9.6"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 16.1(b): at least 21 days before the date set for the
/// scheduling conference, the parties meet to discuss and report on all
/// Fed. R. Civ. P. 16 and 26(f) matters.
deadline parties-meeting-period: 21.days before SchedulingConference() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 16.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 16.1(c): the parties jointly submit the written report on their
/// meeting no later than 14 days before the date set for the scheduling
/// conference.
deadline meeting-report-period: 14.days before SchedulingConference() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 16.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 16.2(b): where the judicial officer requires counsel to confer
/// before a case-management conference, their statement is filed no later
/// than 7 days before the conference.
deadline case-management-statement-period: 7.days before CaseManagementConference() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 16.2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 16.7(a): unless the trial judge orders otherwise, counsel and
/// unrepresented parties meet to negotiate settlement, and make the Fed.
/// R. Civ. P. 26(a)(3) disclosures, no later than 21 days before the final
/// pretrial conference.
deadline pretrial-meeting-period: 21.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 16.7(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 16.7(b): unless the trial judge orders otherwise, the proposed
/// pretrial order is filed no later than 7 days before the final pretrial
/// conference.
deadline proposed-pretrial-order-period: 7.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 16.7(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 26.1(a): unless ordered or stipulated otherwise, the Fed. R.
/// Civ. P. 26(a)(1) disclosures are made no later than 30 days after the
/// Fed. R. Civ. P. 26(f) meeting.
deadline initial-disclosures-period: 30.days after PartiesMeeting() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 26.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 26.1(b)(1): unless ordered or stipulated otherwise, the party
/// bearing the burden of proof on an issue makes its Fed. R. Civ. P.
/// 26(a)(2)(A)-(B) disclosures no later than 60 days before the discovery
/// completion date.
deadline burden-expert-disclosure-period: 60.days before DiscoveryCompletion() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 26.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 26.1(b)(2): the party not bearing the burden of proof on an
/// issue makes its expert disclosures no later than 30 days before the
/// discovery completion date.
deadline responding-expert-disclosure-period: 30.days before DiscoveryCompletion() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 26.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 26.1(b)(3): rebuttal expert disclosures are made no later than
/// 14 days before the discovery completion date.
deadline rebuttal-expert-disclosure-period: 14.days before DiscoveryCompletion() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 26.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 33.1(c): interrogatories ordered answered over objection are
/// answered within 14 days of the order, unless the court directs or the
/// parties stipulate otherwise.
deadline interrogatory-answers-period: 14.days after InterrogatoryAnswersOrdered() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 33.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 34.1(c): document requests ordered answered over objection are
/// answered within 14 days of the order, unless the court directs or the
/// parties stipulate otherwise.
deadline document-answers-period: 14.days after DocumentAnswersOrdered() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 34.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 36.1(b): when a request for admission is held proper over
/// objection, the matter is deemed admitted unless the party served with it
/// serves a denial or a statement why it cannot admit or deny within 14
/// days of the order.
deadline admission-statement-period: 14.days after AdmissionRequestHeldProper() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 36.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 37.1(c): a motion to compel or other motion in aid of discovery
/// not filed within 30 days after the response or disclosure was due is
/// waived; the court for good cause, or the parties by a stipulation filed
/// under LR Civ P 11.2, may extend the period if the scheduling order is
/// not disturbed.
deadline motion-to-compel-period: 30.days after DiscoveryResponseDue() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 37.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 41.1: after notice that an action will be dismissed, good cause
/// for retaining it on the docket is shown within 30 days after the date of
/// the notice, or the judicial officer may dismiss it.
deadline retention-cause-period: 30.days after DismissalNoticeGiven() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 41.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 51.1: in jury cases, proposed jury instructions, special
/// interrogatories and a verdict form are submitted to the judicial officer
/// not less than 7 days before the trial date.
deadline jury-instructions-period: 7.days before TrialDate() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 51.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 52.1: in cases tried to the court, proposed findings of fact
/// and conclusions of law are submitted to the judicial officer 14 days
/// before trial.
deadline proposed-findings-period: 14.days before TrialDate() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 52.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 54.1: the prevailing party prepares a bill of costs within 30
/// days after entry of the final judgment.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 54.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 54.1: specific objections to the bill of costs are filed within
/// 14 days after its service.
deadline costs-objection-period: 14.days after BillOfCostsServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 54.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR Civ P 54.1: a response to the objections is filed within 7 days of
/// their service.
deadline costs-objection-response-period: 7.days after CostsObjectionsServed() counted_by frcp6-west-virginia cite "S.D. W. Va. LR Civ P 54.1"
{
  forum frcp
}
